 "phase": "M8: streaming music on Android (held on branch exp/memory-loading-m8 for the user's decision)",
 "change": "NTSDMusicDecoder: CAF parsed in place (no copy of the file), init(mapping:) maps the file (read instead when it ends within 64 bytes of a page edge), Reader decodes ALAC packets on demand from any frame (checks frame length and packet coverage). NTSDAndroidMusicPCM decodes on the AAudio callback outside its lock and commits only when the position did not move; a refused track plays silence and reports androidMusicError once, as before. AAudio underruns by stream kind reported with androidPresent.",
 "profile": "RAM audit: the Android player held the whole decoded track (Int16) and read the whole file; music on against off cost +24-34 MiB PSS in a match, up to +94 MiB at the peak.",
 "review": "Independent review: OK; follow-ups applied in M8b (underrun counts, mapping guard at page edges, Reader frame-length/coverage checks, asynchronous error for a refused track, a priming test).",
 "notes": "Gate ml-m8 (first version) and ml-m8b (with the follow-ups), both against ml-l20 with music and sounds playing. ml-m8b: peak RSS+swap 560-573 (median 568) against 615-621 (618) MiB; end PSS 520-561 (522) against 577-581 (579) MiB; load 5.54-5.65 against 5.52-5.81 s and launch to loaded 12.62-12.77 against 12.78-12.90 s (overlapping); main and render ms per tick overlapping; whole process CPU from launch to the match end 91.4-92.1 against 94.6-94.9 s; underruns 0 (effects and music). Measurably higher: the AudioTrack threads 1.69-1.72 against 1.16-1.22 ms per tick (process 27.12-27.38 against 26.72-26.86) and 3.85-3.91 against 2.83-2.86 s cumulative: the decode moved from a whole-track burst at each track's start to the music callback while it plays. Under the user's rule (no measurable cost on any game thread or the audio path) this is a memory-for-CPU trade for the user to decide, so it is not merged into the loop's branch.",
